aff may not use a name or pronouns that \"do not align with the pupil's biological sex without … written authorization from the pupil's parent or legal guardian.\" That is a single-subject bill, and its operative section matches rung 5 and goes further than rung 4's notice-only rule. The No side was 45%, so it is not near-unanimous. The chair rests on this one instrument, so code should compute it as `single-source`.\n- **Supporting passages that do not set the chair:** Bradley also voted Aye on the two Parent's Bill of Rights bills, AB 963 (2022, 19–12) and AB 510 (2024, 19–12 and 22–10 respectively). I coded both `multi-subject`. Each bill lists 15–16 parental rights, and the one on names and pronouns (\"The right to determine the names and pronouns used for the child while at school\") points the same way but does not on its own require staff to get permission.\n- **One gap in the bill text:** the AB 103 text in the sources is the version as introduced. I put the enrolled or as-concurred text in `needs_source`, to confirm (4)(b) wasn't amended before the Senate vote.\n- **Two things a reviewer should see:**\n  - **Line number in the quote:** the operative text has line numbers mixed into it. The `provision_quote` copies the page exactly, so it includes a line number: \"…biological sex without 9 written authorization…\".\n  - **Seating:** I coded every passage `in-term` because the vote pages show him in the Senate, but his term dates on file are \"unknown\", so code can't confirm his seating date.\n- **No quotes:** the sources contain none of his own words, so the row has no quotes.","ttft_ms":24258,"type":"result","duration_ms":50489,"uuid":"722c2d13-f625-485b-a371-e8666bda8c8c","ttft_stream_ms":1591,"time_to_request_ms":77,"first_content_frame_ms":1591,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
